> work, voting is the second-best way."

Interesting point of view, and the rest of Dale's post was quite good.  
I look at it a bit differently, though:

  "A market is what you do when you have individual choice.
  Voting is what you do when you're forced to agree on a common solution."

And since it's usually better to have free choice than to be forced
into a group solution, markets win where they apply, and it's very 
Extropian to seek to unbundle decisions to increase individual choice
over collective action.

